- NIST Digital Library of Mathematical Functions, §10.40 Asymptotic Expansions for Large Argument (Modified Bessel Functions), https://dlmf.nist.gov/10.40
- The mpmath development team (2023), mpmath: a Python library for arbitrary-precision floating-point arithmetic, version 1.3.0, https://mpmath.org
- A. Meurer and others (2017), SymPy: symbolic computing in Python, PeerJ Computer Science, 3, e103. https://doi.org/10.7717/peerj-cs.103
- W. P. Johnson (2002), The Curious History of Faa di Bruno's Formula, The American Mathematical Monthly, 109(3), 217–234. https://doi.org/10.2307/2695352
- [4] A. Meurer and others (2017), SymPy: symbolic computing in Python, PeerJ Computer Science, 3, e103. https://doi.org/10.7717/peerj-cs.103
- [5] W. P. Johnson (2002), The Curious History of Faa di Bruno's Formula, The American Mathematical Monthly, 109(3), 217–234. https://doi.org/10.2307/2695352
*/
